>> title: Thai Red Curry Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: thai, chiles, paste, lemongrass, curry
>> counters: Thai Kitchen
>> aka: gaeng dang, gaeng ped, kaeng phet, red curry paste, prik gaeng ped
>> pairs-with: coconut-rice
>> servings: 8
>> time: 45 min
>> slack: narrow — two minutes is the only heat in the recipe, so a scorched cumin seed is in every curry built on this jar
>> step.1: soak 20 min, drain and chop
>> step.2: toast 2 min, grind in a mortar
>> step.3: pound to a fibrous paste
>> step.4: pound in
>> step.5: work in

Soak @dried long red chiles{10}(stemmed and seeded) in @warm water{1%cup}(240 mL) for ~{20%min}, then drain and chop them.

Toast @coriander seeds{1%Tbs}, @cumin seeds{1%tsp}, and @white peppercorns{1%tsp} in a dry #skillet{} over medium heat for ~{2%min}, then grind them to a powder in a #mortar{}.

Pound @&(~2)soaked chiles{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @lemongrass{3%stalks}(tender parts only, thinly sliced), @galangal{1%Tbs}(peeled and chopped), and @makrut lime zest{1%tsp} to a fibrous paste.

Pound @garlic{8%cloves} and @shallots{4}(chopped) into @&(~1)paste{}.

Work @&(~3)ground spices{} and @shrimp paste{1%Tbs}(kapi) into @&(~1)paste{} until it is smooth and glossy.
